WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.372
That evening the students gathered in the schoolroom.

2
00:00:15.373 --> 00:00:18.026
They were talking about Miss Minchin.

3
00:00:18.027 --> 00:00:25.630
She had been angry ever since she returned from the house next door, but the students didn't know why.

4
00:00:25.631 --> 00:00:29.208
Ermengarde rushed into the room with a note in her hand.

5
00:00:29.209 --> 00:00:35.730
"Sara sent a note!" she exclaimed. "Her fortune has been given back to her.

6
00:00:35.731 --> 00:00:39.616
She's going to live with the gentleman next door!"

7
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:45.745
"What? How did this happen?" the girls asked eagerly.

8
00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:49.483
Everyone wanted to hear more from Ermengarde.

9
00:00:49.484 --> 00:00:53.146
Meanwhile little Lottie burst into tears.

10
00:00:53.147 --> 00:00:56.625
She wanted Sara to stay at the school!

11
00:00:56.626 --> 00:01:01.724
"Sara says there really were diamond mines," Ermengarde went on.

12
00:01:01.725 --> 00:01:07.636
"They were filled with millions of diamonds, and she owns half of them.

13
00:01:07.637 --> 00:01:12.329
She's invited me to visit her tomorrow, and I am going!"

14
00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:16.602
The girls chattered loudly about this news.

15
00:01:16.603 --> 00:01:23.550
Miss Minchin heard their noise and thought about scolding them, but she was not in the mood.

16
00:01:23.551 --> 00:01:31.488
Becky also heard them. She crept upstairs earlier than usual.

17
00:01:31.489 --> 00:01:38.221
"Well, that's the end of that," she said to herself.

18
00:01:38.222 --> 00:01:43.413
Her eyes filled with tears as she climbed the last flight of stairs.

19
00:01:43.414 --> 00:01:48.955
She wanted to have one last look at the beautiful things in Sara's room.

20
00:01:48.956 --> 00:01:53.171
"No more fire or rosy lamp," she thought.

21
00:01:53.172 --> 00:01:58.576
"No more supper or anyone telling me stories all night long."

22
00:01:58.577 --> 00:02:02.989
She choked back a sob as she opened the door.

23
00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:09.812
But then she let out a low cry. A fire was blazing—and there stood Ram Dass.

24
00:02:09.813 --> 00:02:13.539
"Miss Sara did not forget you," he said.

25
00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.137
"Tomorrow you will go next door to live as her maid."

26
00:02:17.138 --> 00:02:21.831
"What?" Becky could not believe what she was hearing.

27
00:02:21.832 --> 00:02:25.274
"And here's some supper," said Ram Dass.

28
00:02:25.275 --> 00:02:30.136
"Oh, thank you!" Becky shouted happily.

29
00:02:30.137 --> 00:02:35.528
As time passed, Sara became very close friends with Mr. Carrisford.

30
00:02:35.529 --> 00:02:41.738
The gentleman had never had a companion whom he liked as much as he liked Sara!

31
00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:45.545
One evening they were sitting together as usual.

32
00:02:45.546 --> 00:02:51.961
Mr. Carrisford was reading. Sara was staring into the fire.

33
00:02:51.962 --> 00:02:55.453
"What are you thinking about, Sara?" he asked.

34
00:02:55.454 --> 00:02:59.193
She looked up, her cheeks bright pink.

35
00:02:59.194 --> 00:03:03.370
"I was remembering a day when I was hungry."

36
00:03:03.371 --> 00:03:07.926
"You were hungry many days," Mr. Carrisford replied.

37
00:03:07.927 --> 00:03:10.933
"Which hungry day was it?"

38
00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:14.384
"The day when I gave the buns to the beggar girl."

39
00:03:14.385 --> 00:03:20.271
Sara told him about finding money in the sloppy mud outside the bakery.

40
00:03:20.272 --> 00:03:23.194
"You say that I have so much money now.

41
00:03:23.195 --> 00:03:27.248
Do you think I could use some to help the poor?"

42
00:03:27.249 --> 00:03:31.852
"What would you do?" Mr. Carrisford asked softly.

43
00:03:31.853 --> 00:03:38.394
Sara hesitated. "I'd like the baker to feed any hungry children she sees.

44
00:03:38.395 --> 00:03:41.604
Then she could send the bill to me."

45
00:03:41.605 --> 00:03:47.993
Mr. Carrisford instantly nodded. "That's a wonderful idea!"

46
00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:53.588
The next day Sara and Mr. Carrisford visited the baker.

47
00:03:53.589 --> 00:03:58.420
The woman looked closely at Sara. "Have we met before?"

48
00:03:58.421 --> 00:04:04.457
Her friendly face lit up. "I feel that I remember you, but I cannot quite—"

49
00:04:04.458 --> 00:04:10.512
"You once gave me six buns when I could only pay for four!" said Sara.

50
00:04:10.513 --> 00:04:15.684
"And then you gave five of them to a beggar child!" the woman replied.

51
00:04:15.685 --> 00:04:22.092
"I always remembered that." The baker turned to Mr. Carrisford.

52
00:04:22.093 --> 00:04:25.465
"There aren't many children who would do that."

53
00:04:25.466 --> 00:04:31.654
She looked closely at Sara again. "Excuse me, miss, but you look different.

54
00:04:31.655 --> 00:04:35.932
Your cheeks are rosy now, and you appear quite healthy."

55
00:04:35.933 --> 00:04:41.483
"My life has changed," Sara said.

56
00:04:41.484 --> 00:04:45.015
"I was wondering if you could do something for me."

57
00:04:45.016 --> 00:04:50.168
She explained her plan involving poor children and free buns.

58
00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:54.454
The woman watched her, listening with an astonished face.

59
00:04:54.455 --> 00:04:59.195
"Why, I'd be happy to do that," said the baker.

60
00:04:59.196 --> 00:05:02.826
"In fact you've already inspired me.

61
00:05:02.827 --> 00:05:07.780
You looked so cold and hungry, and yet you gave away those buns.

62
00:05:07.781 --> 00:05:11.402
I've often fed poor children since that day."

63
00:05:11.403 --> 00:05:16.294
"I wonder where that beggar girl is now," Sara said.

64
00:05:16.295 --> 00:05:20.783
"Why, she's right here!" the baker replied.

65
00:05:20.784 --> 00:05:24.329
"I told her to come back whenever she was hungry.

66
00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:28.522
I gave her odd jobs and she turned out to be a good worker.

67
00:05:28.523 --> 00:05:30.732
Her name is Anne."

68
00:05:30.733 --> 00:05:35.184
The baker went into the back room and brought Anne out.

69
00:05:35.185 --> 00:05:38.276
Anne was healthy and well fed now.

70
00:05:38.277 --> 00:05:41.924
The two girls stood looking at each other for a minute.

71
00:05:41.925 --> 00:05:45.813
Then Sara held out her hand, and Anne took it.

72
00:05:45.814 --> 00:05:49.898
"I'm so glad that you're doing well," said Sara.

73
00:05:49.899 --> 00:05:53.694
"The baker is going to give buns to poor children.

74
00:05:53.695 --> 00:05:57.368
Perhaps you'd like to be the one who hands out the food.

75
00:05:57.369 --> 00:06:01.309
After all, you know what it's like to be hungry."

76
00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:06.910
"Oh yes, miss," said Anne. "I'd like that very much."

77
00:06:06.911 --> 00:06:10.372
The little princess was very pleased.

78
00:06:10.373 --> 00:06:15.630
"You'll quickly discover what I have discovered," she told Anne.

79
00:06:15.631 --> 00:06:24.398
"There is great joy in giving."
